- research/seo-metadata/link-preview-rendering-by-platform -- what each platform shows: X lays only the title over the image's bottom edge, LinkedIn drops the description, Slack shrinks the image to about 360 px wide, Meta caches images by address, keep key content clear of the edges; grounds the legibility and fit decisions.
- research/seo-metadata/2026-10-27-search-ready-saas-site -- §4 Open Graph: per-page images beat one shared image for shares of specific pages, 1200×630 with alt text; grounds the page-card layout.
- .aide/session.aide decisions #37 and #42 -- a per-page share image in this cycle, and rendering driven by the pre-deploy build step from the one site page list; grounds the build-time and page-records decisions.
